Download the Windows installer
Go to the UB Mannheim build (best Windows version):
https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki
Under “Download”, grab the latest tesseract-ocr-w64-setup-…exe.
Run the installer
Accept defaults unless you want a different folder.
When prompted for “Additional language data”, you can keep English only (default) or add more languages.
Add Tesseract to your PATH
Default install path is C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR.
Open Windows Search → “Environment Variables” → “Edit the system environment variables”.
Click “Environment Variables…”.
Under “System variables”, select Path → “Edit” → “New”.
Paste C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR.
Click OK on each dialog to save.
Verify installation
Open a new PowerShell window.
Run: tesseract --version
You should see version info. If “command not found” appears, re-check the PATH.
Install Poppler for PDF support (needed by pdf2image)
Download from: https://github.com/oschwartz10612/poppler-windows/releases
Extract, e.g. to C:\poppler
Add C:\poppler\Library\bin to your PATH using the same steps as above.
Verify: open PowerShell, run pdfinfo -v. Should show version.
Restart your server
Stop the current uvicorn process (Ctrl+C in that terminal).
Start it again: python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload
This ensures the app sees Tesseract/Poppler on PATH.
Test OCR
Upload a sample scanned image (JPG/PNG) via http://127.0.0.1:8000.
Check logs for Extracted … characters messages, and confirm the document details populate.